# gd-plug-plus

Enhanced addon manager for Godot 4.x with built-in UI. Repo: `huzz-open/gd-plug-plus`.

## Core Data Files

### addons.json (user data — NOT in repo)

Tracks all installed addons. Managed by `AddonData.gd`. Gitignored in the plugin directory.

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1.0,
  "repos": {
    "user/repo-name": {
      "url": "https://...",
      "addons": [
        {
          "name": "...",
          "addon_dir": "addons/...",
          "branch": "main",
          "commit": "abc123...",
          "installed": true,
          ...
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### addon_index.json (community catalog — IN repo)

"App store" directory for the Available tab. Ships with the plugin and updates via self-update. A plain JSON array:

```json
[
  {
    "url": "https://...",
    "addons": [
      {
        "name": "...",
        "addon_dir": "addons/...",
        "branch": "main",
        "description": "...",
        "author": "...",
        "type": "plugin"
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

## Key Architecture

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `AddonData.gd` | Data layer — addons.json CRUD, version logic, conflict detection |
| `GitManager.gd` | Git operations — clone, checkout, fetch, copy, scan |
| `AddonManager.gd` | UI controller — install/update/uninstall flows, tree rendering |
| `SelectorPopup.gd` | Branch/tag/commit selector popup |

## Self-Update

gd-plug-plus tracks itself in `addons.json` (auto-registered on first startup via `_ensure_self_tracked()`). Updates flow through the same mechanism as any other addon. The plugin cannot be uninstalled through its own UI.

When self-updating:
- `addon_index.json` gets updated (new community entries)
- `addons.json` is preserved (not in the repo, so copy doesn't touch it)
- A reload toast is shown after self-update completes
